. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
.         
.         *       Our measure for support for gender quality is agreement with 
> the question: plh0395i04--The assignment of gender is not important for the d
> evelopment of a person. 
.         
.         *       Our data are at the child level, for child births after the f
> irst. We control for the gender of prior children, as a way of controlling fo
> r the likelihood of a child being a girl (due to propensity for a particular 
> couple to produce female children). We also add a few controls to reduce erro
> r variance: plh0258_h – Categorial religious affiliation plg0267 – Categorica
> l Educational Attainment plb0471_h – Gross Income prev year hgnuts1 -categori
> cal federal state
.         
.         *       We cluster at the parent-level
. 
. 
.         * As an example, and for illustrative purposes we consider a: linear 
> OLS regression
. 
.         * For illustrative purposes, let's further assume that having a job t
> hat requires hard manual labor (plb0085) is a good measure of support for gen
> der equality (hypothesis 1), 
.         * if having a job with less manual labor, the respondent is more like
> ly to support gender equality.
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with plb0085 a
> s dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as independent variabl
> e
.         
.         
. 
